nal Requirements\\n42|4.1 Source Code Management (SCM)\\n43|The solution shall provide:\\n44|Distributed version\\n45|control repositories \\n46|Branching, merging, and\\n47|pull/merge request workflows \\n48|Role-based access\\n49|control for repositories \\n50|Web-based repository\\n51|management interface \\n52|Full audit trail of code\\n53|changes \\n54|4.2 CI/CD Pipeline Management\\n55|The solution shall support:\\n56|Declarative pipeline\\n57|definitions (e.g., YAML-based) \\n58|Automated build, test,\\nand deployment workflows \\n59|Event-based triggers\\n60|(code commits, schedules, API calls) \\n61|Parallel and scalable\\n62|pipeline execution \\n63|Artifact generation and\\n64|retention \\n65|4.3 Project and Work Management\\n66|The platform shall include:\\n67|Issue and ticket\\n68|management system \\n69|Agile boards (Scrum and\\n70|Kanban) \\n71|Sprint and milestone\\n72|tracking \\n73|Collaboration features\\n74|(comments, mentions, notifications) \\n75|4.4 Package and Artifact Repository\\n76|The solution shall provide:\\n77|Support for multiple\\n78|package formats (containers, binaries, libraries) \\n79|Version-controlled\\n80|artifact storage \\n81|Dependency caching and\\n82|proxy capabilities \\n83|4.5 User and Access Management\\n84|The platform shall support:\\n85|Role-Based Access\\n86|Control (RBAC) \\n87|Integration with\\n88|enterprise identity systems (LDAP / Active Directory) \\n89|Multi-project and\\n90|multi-team isolation \\n91|Comprehensive audit\\n92|logging \\n93|5. Advanced DevOps Requirements\\n94|5.1 DevSecOps Capabilities\\n95|The solution shall include:\\n96|Static code security\\n97|analysis \\n98|Dynamic application\\n99|security testing \\n100|Open-source dependency\\n101|vulnerability scanning \\n102|Secret detection\\n103|mechanisms \\n104|Container security\\n105|scanning \\n106|5.2 Infrastructure as Code (IaC)\\n107|The solution shall:\\n108|Support infrastructure\\n109|provisioning through code \\n110|Enable version control\\n111|of infrastructure definitions \\n112|Integrate IaC into CI/CD\\n113|pipelines \\n114|5.3 Deployment and Environment Management\\n115|The platform shall provide:\\n116|Multi-environment\\n117|lifecycle management (Dev, Test, UAT, Production) \\n118|Deployment strategies\\n119|including: \\n120|Blue/Green \\n121|Canary \\n122|Rolling deployments \\n123|Environment-specific\\n124|configuration control \\n125|5.4 Monitoring and Observability\\n126|The solution shall support:\\n127|Pipeline monitoring and\\n128|execution tracking \\n129|Integration with logging\\n130|and monitoring systems \\n131|Alerting and\\n132|notification mechanisms \\n133|Operational dashboards \\n134|5.5 API and Integration\\n135|The platform shall include:\\n136|Comprehensive REST APIs \\n137|Webhook support for\\n138|integrations \\n139|Compatibility with\\n140|third-party tools and cloud services \\n141|6. Enterprise Requirements\\n142|6.1 Governance and Compliance\\n143|The solution shall provide:\\n144|Policy enforcement for\\n145|pipelines and deployments \\n146|Approval workflows and\\n147|release gates \\n148|Compliance reporting and\\n149|audit trails \\n150|6.2 Analytics and Reporting\\n151|The platform shall include:\\n152|DevOps performance\\n153|metrics (e.g., deployment frequency, lead time) \\n154|Pipeline efficiency\\n155|analytics \\n156|Team productivity\\n157|insights \\n158|6.3 High Availability and Scalability\\n159|The solution shall:\\n160|Support clustered\\n161|deployment architecture \\n162|Enable horizontal\\n163|scaling of workloads \\n164|Provide load balancing\\n165|and failover mechanisms \\n166|6.4 Backup and Disaster Recovery\\n167|The platform shall include:\\n168|Automated backup\\n169|capabilities \\n170|Point-in-time recovery \\n171|Disaster recovery\\n172|options across sites \\n173|6.5 AI-Driven Capabilities (Optional)\\n174|Vendors are encouraged to provide:\\n175|AI-assisted code\\n176|analysis and recommendations \\n177|Predictive pipeline\\n178|failure detection \\n179|Intelligent automation\\n180|and optimization features \\n181|7. Deployment Requirements\\n182|The solution must be\\n183|deployed on-premises at Roxy Data Center \\n184|Support for private\\n185|cloud or hybrid architecture is preferred \\n186|Must align with MOE\\n187|infrastructure standards (compute, storage, network) \\n188|8. Security Requirements\\n189|The solution must:\\n190|Ensure encryption of\\n191|data in transit and at rest \\n192|Support Single Sign-On\\n193|(SSO), OAuth, and SAML \\n194|Provide fine-grained\\n195|access controls \\n196|Maintain detailed audit\\n197|logs for all activities \\n198|9. Operational Requirements\\n199|Web-based user interface\\n200|CLI and API access \\n201|Automated patching and\\n202|upgrade mechanisms \\n203|Role-based dashboards\\n204|and views \\n205|10. Licensing Requirements\\n206|Vendors must provide:\\n207|Flexible licensing model\\n208|based on: \\n209|Number of users \\n210|Compute/pipeline\\n211|capacity \\n212|Storage usage \\n213|Tiered licensing options\\n214|(Core / Advanced / Enterprise) \\n215|Clear definition of\\n216|included features per tier \\n217|11. Deliverables\\n218|The vendor shall deliver:\\n219|Fully deployed DevOps\\n220|platform at Roxy Data Center \\n221|Software licenses and\\n222|activation \\n223|Configuration and\\n224|integration with MOE systems \\n225|Technical documentation \\n226|Training sessions for\\n227|MOE teams \\n228|Support and maintenance\\n229|services'''\n# split lines\nlines = content.split('\\n')\nplain_lines=[re.sub(r'^\\d+\\|', '', l) for l in lines]\nplain_text='\\n'.join(plain_lines)\nprint(json.dumps({'text': plain_text, 'length': len(plain_text)}))"}
